# Pointing clients at Headscale

Create a user and a reusable auth key on the server:

    docker compose exec headscale headscale users create sealedstack
    docker compose exec headscale headscale preauthkeys create --user sealedstack --reusable

Then, on each client, log in to this control server instead of Tailscale's:

    tailscale up --login-server {{ mesh_headscale_server_url }} --authkey <key>

The node keys and database live in the `headscale-data` volume; back it up with
the rest of the state. `{{ mesh_headscale_server_url }}` must resolve to this
host and terminate TLS in front of port {{ mesh_headscale_listen_port }}.
